# Dotted tokens in the shipped text that are NOT .claude/ds-config.json keys, so
# scripts/check-config-keys.py does not require them in schemas/seam-registry.json.
# One token per line, then its reason. A real config key never belongs here: register it.
user.login            a GitHub API field (review-thread authors)
github.actor          a GitHub Actions context value
attachment.id         a DevStride API field in a worked example
statusLine.command    a Claude Code settings.json key, not a ds-config key
ci.concurrency        a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
ci.productionTreeSkip a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
ci.policyCheck        a per-workflow fact setup's CI detection records in its report
record.pluginVersion  a field of the clearance provider's `status --json` record, not a ds-config key
heartbeat.phase       a field of the step runner's run answer (the story claim's phase), not a ds-config key
heartbeat.stage       a field of the step runner's run answer (the ship-intent stage), not a ds-config key
heartbeat.shipIntent  a field of the step runner's run answer (the ship-intent request), not a ds-config key
instructions.text     a field of the step runner's run answer (a repository step's committed text), not a ds-config key
put.command           a field of the step runner's fetch-skill answer (the library skill helper's command), not a ds-config key
put.request           a field of the step runner's fetch-skill answer (the library skill save request), not a ds-config key
skill.file            a field of the step runner's run answer (a library step's verified saved copy), not a ds-config key
